{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/non_tail_recursion_1.march","start_line":33,"start_col":27,"end_line":33,"end_col":34,"message":"Function `size` is structurally recursive but not tail-recursive. If the recursive call is the direct argument of a constructor in tail position, tail-recursion-modulo-cons compiles it to a loop with no extra stack (it always runs). Otherwise it uses O(depth) stack space and deep input can overflow the stack — consider an accumulator parameter.","code":"non_tail_recursion","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"RECURSION"}
